WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:04.136
-The last few days
of Donald Trump's presidency

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.438
have been very revealing.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.239
He has, among other things,
feuded with the press,

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:09.442
admitted that being president
is harder than he thought,

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.211
praised authoritarian rulers,

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.679
and made bizarre comments
about the Civil War.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.948
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:19.319 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.587
As you may recall,

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.589
Trump's positions on most issues
during the campaign

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:24.857
weren't all that clear.

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:27.393
But there was one thing
he was very clear about,

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:30.329
and that was that being
President would be easy.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:31.664
-We're going to make America
great again.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.033
It's gonna be easy.
It's gonna be easy.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.302
It's so --
it's going to be easy.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.004
Believe me,
the jobs are coming back, folks.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.172
That's gonna be so easy.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:42.509
You're going to have
such great health care

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:46.946
at a tiny fraction of the cost,
and it's gonna be so easy.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.581
And they don't understand it.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.117
They said, "But how do you
get them to pay?"

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.619
I said, "It's so easy."
And you understand.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:56.088
Okay? Rely on me.
So easy. That's so easy.

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.658
-People
who are actually reliable

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.728
don't have to say the words,
"Rely on me."

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.763
If you ask our buddy to pick you
up from the airport

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.431
and he says, "Rely on me,"

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.935
get ready for dinner
at Cinnabon.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.237
Of course,
the story of the first 100 days

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.306
has been Trump's
childlike naiveté

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.640
colliding with reality.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.009
In fact, Trump has
without shame admitted

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.212
that basic aspects of the job
have turned out

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.714
to be harder than he thought,
like health care

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.549
or China's relationship
with North Korea.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:26.085 line:0%
-It's an unbelievably complex
subject.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:29.022 line:0%
Nobody knew that health care
could be so complicated.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.957
-Mr. Trump said
he told his Chinese counterpart

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.225
he believed Beijing could easily

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.793
take care
of the North Korea threat.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.228
Mr. Xi then explained the
history of China and Korea.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:38.331
Mr. Trump said, and I'm quoting
the president here,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.401
"After listening for 10 minutes,
I realized it's not so easy."

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.503
-The president is literally

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:47.473
being tutored
by foreign leaders.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.174
[ Imitating Trump ] And after
he taught me the history

00:01:49.174 --> 00:01:50.242
of China and North Korea,

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.811
he helped me
with my math homework,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.579
which was very...

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.647
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.716
[ Normal voice ] And while
he's at it, maybe President Xi

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.084
could give Trump an American
history lesson, too,

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:01.154
because today
when Trump was asked about

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.823
his supposed model for
the presidency, Andrew Jackson,

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:07.360
he went on a bizarre tangent
about the Civil War and Jackson,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.497
who died 16 years
before the war started.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.648
-Yeah.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.558
-Yeah.

00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:42.595
People don't ask that question.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.131
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:49.401
No one ever asked
why was there the Civil War.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:51.403
And who can forget
those searing letters

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:53.172
from soldiers
on the battlefield?

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.775 line:0%
[ Somber violin music plays ]

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:29.341
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:33.545
So Trump clearly, clearly

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.581
does not have a firm grasp

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:36.982
on the basic aspects
of being president,

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:38.751
let alone basic facts
about American history.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.687
And now he's essentially
admitting

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.121
that he's in over his head,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.656
telling a reporter
that he didn't expect

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.491
the the job of President
to be this hard.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.951
You thought the presidency
would be easier

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:15.954
than being a game show host?

00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:18.057
There's a reason Abraham Lincoln
is on the 5

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.928
instead of Alex Trebek.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:26.865
Although I have to say
that this,

00:04:26.865 --> 00:04:29.702
this is the most absurd part
of Trump's answer.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:33.205
-I'm a details-oriented person.
I think you would say that.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:36.041
-No.

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:38.677
I would not say that.

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:41.681
No one thinks details
are your strong suit.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:43.583
And I'm not even talking
about the little details.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:46.151
I'm talking about things like
why did the Civil War happen

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:50.690
or, you know, which country
did I just bomb?

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:55.494 line:0%
-We just launched 59 missiles
heading to Iraq.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:56.963 line:0%
-Headed to Syria.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.531 line:0%
-Yes, heading towards Syria.

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:01.800
-[ As Trump ] Yes. Yeah, Syria.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.103
But you know, Iraq.
Spoiler alert.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.006
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:12.245
[ Normal voice ]
Now, you might think --

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.545
You might think a president

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:15.914
as unqualified as Trump
would show some humility.

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:18.017
Instead, he spent
the last few days as usual

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.018
attacking the media.

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:20.819
Today, he abruptly ended
an interview

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:22.388
with CBS's John Dickerson

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.890
after once again making
his baseless claim

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.226
that then-President Obama
had him surveilled

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.127
but refusing to provide
any evidence.

00:05:29.127 --> 00:05:32.130
All Dickerson did was try
to get Trump to explain

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.800
what his own words meant,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.634
but Trump was not having it.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.536
-You saw what happened
with surveillance,

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:40.105
and I think that was
inappropriate.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:41.140
-What does that mean, sir?

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.841
-You can figure that out
yourself.

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:46.145
-The reason I ask is you said
called him sick and bad.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.814
-Look, you can figure it out
yourself.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.349
But you stand by that claim
about him?

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.017
-I don't stand by anything.
I just --

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:53.519
You can take it
the way you want.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.822
-But I'm asking you because you
don't want it to be fake news.

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.223
I want to hear it
from President Trump.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.724
-You don't have to ask me.
-Why not?

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:01.927
-Because I have my own opinions,
you can have your own opinions.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:03.129
-But I want to know
your opinions.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.663
You're the president
of the United States.

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:06.398
-That's enough. Thank you.

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:08.334
Thank you very much.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:12.038
-You know, dramatic exits
are definitely less dramatic

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:16.442
when you stay in the same room
and just sit down.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:19.312
You can't fire me!
I quit!

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.313
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:23.349
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:31.356
Maybe Trump is just frustrated
by the fact

00:06:31.356 --> 00:06:32.658
that despite his many promises,

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.627
he has very little to show
for his first 100 days.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.696
In fact, his only real
accomplishment seems to be

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:39.565
turning the Oval Office into
something of a man cave.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.033
A reporter for
the<i> Financial Times</i>

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.336
relayed this anecdote from
a recent interview with Trump.

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.388
[ As Trump ] No, no, no,
that's not the nuclear button.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.690
The nuclear button
is right next to it.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.392
It's also small and red,
but I remember which one it is

00:07:07.392 --> 00:07:09.261
because it's on the right,
and I have the right

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:10.930
to use nuclear weapons.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.798
Of course, I also have the right

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:14.066
to have a Coke
in the middle of the day

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.200
because I'm the president

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.869
and I don't have to worry
about it the sugar

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:18.270
because I have the best dentist.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.707
I mean, this guy, he is amazing,
and he's right about everything,

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.675
which is why I keep
a right button

00:07:23.675 --> 00:07:26.078
to the right of my Coke button
that calls my dentist.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:27.680
You want me to call him
right now?

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:32.151
[ Applause ]

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.920
[ Normal voice ]
So Trump doesn't seem

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.388
to have much knowledge of

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:39.491
or interest in things like
governing or American history.

00:07:39.491 --> 00:07:41.560
But there's one thing Trump
is very interested in,

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.195
and that's his own
electoral victory

00:07:43.195 --> 00:07:45.864
because Trump called reporters
into his office

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:48.367
to discuss the accomplishments
of his first 100 days,

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.936
the only actual accomplishment
he had to offer

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:52.604
was the act of becoming
President,

00:07:52.604 --> 00:07:54.907
an accomplishment he bragged
about in the middle of a
conversation

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:57.276
about Chinese president
Xi Jinping.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.077
-We were talking,
as I mentioned earlier,

00:07:59.077 --> 00:08:01.547
about President Xi
and that relationship,

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:04.249
and then he sort of
interrupted himself

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:08.954
and handed out this map
of the electoral college

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:11.490
and said that these were
the latest figures

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:15.127
of the areas in the country
that he had won in 2016.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.396
And there were three of us
in the interview, as I said,

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.698
and he had a copy
for each of us.

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:22.568
I think he just wanted
to relish in the fact

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:25.471
that this map
looks good for him.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:28.340
And he said,
"The red is obviously us."

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:32.144
And the red are the areas
in the country that he won.

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.478
-[ As Trump ] And in fact,

00:08:33.478 --> 00:08:35.314
I even colored in
the map myself.

00:08:37.382 --> 00:08:39.518
And if you noticed,
I stayed within the lines,

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:42.054
which everyone says
is the hardest part.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.825
And I did it all in under
100 days, which...

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:48.594
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.262
[ Normal voice ] Now, as
troubling as all of that is,

00:08:50.262 --> 00:08:52.031
Trump has also spent
a lot of time lately

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:53.432
praising authoritarian rulers

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:54.867
with terrible
human rights records.

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:56.334
For example, he recently issued
a statement

00:08:56.334 --> 00:08:58.036
congratulating Turkey's
president

00:08:58.036 --> 00:09:00.606
for a referendum that gave him
expansive new powers.

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.007
And in interviews
over the weekend,

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:04.576
Trump praised North Korea's
Kim Jong-un multiple times,

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:06.979
calling him a "pretty smart
cookie" and saying...

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.853
You'd be honored?

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:14.987
[ As Trump ]
He's very misunderstood.

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:16.221
You'd like him.
We should call him.

00:09:16.221 --> 00:09:17.456
I think it's this button.

00:09:21.927 --> 00:09:25.531
And Kim Jong-un wasn't the only
authoritarian

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:26.799
Trump praised this weekend.

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:29.434
On Saturday, he spoke with
President Rodrigo Duterte

00:09:29.434 --> 00:09:30.636
of the Philippines.

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:32.638
Duterte has been accused
of running death squads

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:35.207
and has bragged that he has
personally murdered people,

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.409
like when he said...

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.183
It's stories like that
that earned Duterte

00:09:45.183 --> 00:09:47.486
the nickname "United Airlines."

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.722
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.757
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:57.095
Now, Duterte has since claimed
he was joking.

00:09:57.095 --> 00:09:59.298
Nonetheless, despite his dismal
human rights record,

00:09:59.298 --> 00:10:00.599
the White House
issued a statement saying

00:10:00.599 --> 00:10:02.768
Trump and Duterte
had a very friendly conversation

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.937
and that President Trump
invited President Duterte

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:05.804
to the White House.

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:06.938
So, if you're a journalist

00:10:06.938 --> 00:10:08.941
covering the White House
when Duterte visits,

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.509
and you hear Donald Trump
say this...

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:12.344 line:0%
-Let's give them
a helicopter ride, okay?

00:10:12.344 --> 00:10:13.913
-...run!

00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:18.017
So to recap, a president
who's in over his head

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:19.251
is fighting with the media,

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:21.086
reminiscing about his
election night victory,

00:10:21.086 --> 00:10:23.322
inviting authoritarian rulers to
the White House,

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:25.791
and also maybe doesn't know
why the Civil War happened.

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:27.893
Donald, do you still stand
by your claim

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:29.562
that the presidency
would be easy?

00:10:29.562 --> 00:10:30.662
-I don't stand by anything.

00:10:30.662 --> 00:10:32.765
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:36.035 line:0%
♪♪

